  "item_notes": {
    "1": "Both real US smoke cells have COMPLETE.json, manifest status ok, rc=0, and PASS rows. poll.py configures grade_cell.sh as its Studio worker. grade_hc01.sh invoked that same worker directly; the poll.py watcher/scheduler itself was not invoked.",
    "10": "EXCEPTION (builder ruling 2026-10-08): accepted: API-equivalent cost via levers/cost.py plus an R72-style exception for the remaining emitter gaps, declared before release in MISSING.md (section 'Pre-release declaration'). Outcome and grade fields are complete in the smoke records; fix ticket RUN-RECORD-FIX-TICKET.md sha256 38dc956ded0e11c80b3605424c2d856f6986af651af679cb8710aea6226ebbee.",
    "11": "lint_launchers passes for the expanded manifest; 30 local and deployed dry-run vectors match PLAN and each other by SHA-256. Post-ruling fix (2026-10-08): launcher host check accepted only names starting 'kogen-bench-us' and refused on the real US hostname kogen-bench-us; now also accepts that exact hostname. Launcher sha256 f68e195698083f1d623e34b7b5f5f41b6c5e2639ce2a630f4bb16fb10f8b9d99; plan vectors unchanged (dry-run 885ed104).",
    "2": "The OFF and ON smoke commands were separate sequential bench-rs.py invocations through the HC01 sandbox path.",
    "3": "This checklist job used no credentials, Codex CLI, or refreshing auth client; lane readiness records auth-path stat-only handling and sandbox egress constraints.",
    "4": "EXCEPTION (builder ruling 2026-10-08, relaying the owner's authority): base gate receipt: compile/tests PASS; formatter check fails on the untouched base (pre-existing, arm-symmetric). Evidence: BASE-GATES-US.json sha256 3da8c41571829f6fe99a296ab8d5d835de78dca5ebc3f47e424e65f51582d24d (erase + board: mix format --check-formatted rc 1; compile --warnings-as-errors rc 0; mix test rc 0; syn06 + syn31 all green). Arm-symmetric: both arms start from the identical frozen base in the identical environment. Official grade rows for this route carry hidden-suite outcome fields only (no formatter field), and both smoke cells were official PASS on a syn06 base. Escalate only if found environment-induced and arm-dependent, or if the official grader runs the formatter. Root-cause facts follow after release for the record.",
    "5": "EXCEPTION (builder ruling 2026-10-08): satisfied in intent: the shared root is mandated by the design (DESIGN/LANE-REQUIREMENTS item 1: one binary and commit for both arms, only build.context_packet differs). It's a fresh clone at 1bc2422 with no other use.",
    "6": "Both real smoke cells ran the no-hash kogen intent approve check: approval_check rc 5, followed by hashed approval rc 0 and queue start rc 0.",
    "7": "One sequential dispatcher, lane lock, recognized host-wide active-runner check, STOP checks, and 5,000,000,000-byte floor are in the launcher; current snapshot is recorded below.",
    "8": "DESIGN and DECISION-RULE predate smoke; AMENDMENT-1 records the US host switch before the first HC01 cell.",
    "9": "The smoke wrapper uses the frozen PLAN argv directly; there was no separate brief and cx.sh was not changed."
  },
